{"parentUuid":"9f94c0e5-e3f1-4ea1-b8dc-ae70057fa877","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"1","subject":"Answer the open question with option one","description":"Use the installed companion emulator against the still-open question and submit the user's requested first option, recording the live result.","activeForm":"Answering the open question","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"2","subject":"Remove all answer guards","description":"Change the desktop bridge so no transcript, screen, session, binding, permission-axis, marker, or similar runtime guard can refuse a remotely expressible answer. Preserve only API shape validation needed to encode the selected answer; follow the user's directive that any question visible in the terminal must remain answerable from phone/watch.","activeForm":"Removing all answer guards","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"3","subject":"Verify and ship the guardless path","description":"Add/adjust tests for locked or off-screen desktop operation, run required scoped validation and reviews, commit directly to main, push, and start the full GitHub build for installation later.","activeForm":"Verifying and shipping the guardless path","status":"in_progress","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"4","subject":"Acknowledge companion PTY writes","description":"Add a daemon-backed acknowledged raw-input operation so companion answer writes report success only after session.pty.write succeeds; propagate zero/partial failures honestly and test missing/exited/write-error cases.","activeForm":"Acknowledging companion PTY writes","owner":"pty-ack","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[],"metadata":{"verification":"Daemon/protocol unit tests 28/28; companion suite 263/263; REFERR-GATE clean; pty-daemon bundle builds. Host build/typecheck reach only merged v1.20 dependency/pre-existing errors, zero new acknowledgment diagnostics. DaemonClient integration test added for Linux; local Windows cannot bind Unix .sock (EACCES)."}},{"id":"5","subject":"Make confirmed outcome durable","description":"Stop swallowing confirmed ledger transition failures. Return confirmed only after the durable transition commits; bytes-written persistence failure must become fenced honest unconfirmed behavior without duplicate execution.","activeForm":"Making confirmed outcomes durable","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"6","subject":"Repair transcript unreadable caching","description":"Do not cache transient unreadable transcript verdicts so a later successful read can positively settle a desk-answered question.","activeForm":"Repairing transcript reconciliation caching","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[],"metadata":{"verification":"14 question-lifecycle tests pass; unchanged transcript is rescanned after unreadable and resolves on second pass."}},{"id":"7","subject":"Expose every pending question","description":"Ensure paired phone/watch can discover and fetch every pending captured question regardless of missing session/capability or sidebar curation, while preserving authentication and semantic validation.","activeForm":"Exposing every pending question","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[],"metadata":{"verification":"68 curation/session tests pass. Baseline no-grant tree exposes pending refs through curated-off workspace/project; /v1/question is session/capability ungated but remains paired/sealed/schema validated."}},{"id":"8","subject":"Contain partial-write audit failures","description":"After a durable partial-write unconfirmed outcome, catch/log audit sink failure and return unconfirmed rather than throwing.","activeForm":"Containing partial-write audit failures","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"9","subject":"Restore guardless type safety","description":"Resolve new callback/result diagnostics from synchronous injection and update lease mocks to the current shape without reintroducing guards.","activeForm":"Restoring guardless type safety","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[],"metadata":{"verification":"Host-service typecheck now reports only the two pre-existing terminal.ts diagnostics; 5 guardless tests pass."}},{"id":"10","subject":"Fence ambiguous acknowledged-write failures","description":"Differentiate daemon/PTTY outcomes that provably wrote zero bytes from timeout/disconnect outcomes where the first byte may have landed; ambiguous first-write outcomes must return durable unconfirmed and retain a duplicate fence, never invite retry as zero-write failed.","activeForm":"Fencing ambiguous write outcomes","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"11","subject":"Protect reconcile settlement races","description":"Re-check pending state immediately before transcript reconciliation settles a question, preserving phone provenance/stale terminal state if another path settled it during awaits.","activeForm":"Protecting reconcile settlement races","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"12","subject":"Align heartbeat pending-question counts","description":"Make heartbeat status counts apply the same curated-workspace exception as tree projection for terminals carrying a pending captured question.","activeForm":"Aligning heartbeat question counts","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"13","subject":"Migrate detached PTY protocol safely","description":"Keep v2 ordinary terminal adoption compatible while requiring v3 before acknowledged companion writes; bump daemon package version and verify old-daemon adoption/update detection rather than retaining an unreachable unknown instance.","activeForm":"Migrating detached PTY protocol","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]}],"itemCount":13},"type":"attachment","uuid":"da4d6673-0404-45bc-8ab1-26391c5ee32f","timestamp":"2026-08-10T22:44:39.937Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd"